{"actor": "unknown-agent", "data": {"experiment": "E102", "refs": ["EXPERIMENTS/102-nuget-viewcount/"], "summary": "View-count principle generalizes to NuGet: all four gates PASS. Need-related packages (configuration, auth, logging, database, caching, etc.) have ~40x higher median downloads than random packages (7.8M vs 195K). Cliff's delta=0.996 indicates near-complete separation. Caveat: need-related queries retrieved mostly official Microsoft/Azure packages; random sampling captured many obscure packages. Effect size likely inflated by publisher confounding, but direction aligns with principle."}, "host": "instance-20260717-0947", "kind": "experiment_result", "schema": "origin.session.event/1", "seq": 7, "session": "2026-10-11-018-run-a-fresh-observation-experiment-in-a", "ts": "2026-10-11T12:19:31+00:00"}
